# Grouping (v1)

Source of truth: `Order Grouping Sorter/order-grouping-locks.md`. Do not guess. No definite match → whole order `unmatched`. Chat `--run` does not seed the catalog (catalog step removed 2026-10-20; `approval.mdc`). Still-awaiting orders are not skipped for an earlier shift CSV.

## SKU keys (not universal `resolve_label`)

| Catalog | Key |
|---------|-----|
| CL | **After first dash** → `Custom Label`. **No dash → whole SKU** (`A515`). |
| Plain | **Till last dash** or whole SKU → `SKU` |
| Absolute | **Till last dash** or whole SKU → Absolute Product Data **Stock Code** |
| Packs | **Whole SKU** → `Channel Child SKU` |

Finish gate: SKU contains `plain` / `plainlg` → plain; else CL → printed; else Plain → plain; else Absolute stock code → plain; else Packs → plain; else unmatched. Mixed plain+printed → printed-wins. Mixed printed P vs R → majority printed units; tie → readymade (not unmatched). Mixed supply-method → **Supplier On Demand** (on-demand item arrives later; not unmatched).

Attribute source (separate): Packs whole → else CL after-first (or whole when no dash) → else Plain → else Absolute stock code.

## Intake

Skip `post-order-designs`, tag `00000-Warehouse OOS` (locked 2026-10-09), and tag `1006- PERSONALISED ORDER Listing Error (DW)` (locked 2026-10-14). Tag `1014-ALL-RESEND` only → resend fixed batches `B9000` / `B9050` / `B9040` / `B9100` / `B9150` / `B9200` (locked 2026-10-18; catalog-miss stays `RESEND`). Resend is not held for a missing `1004` tag. Customised (P) piles only with tag **`1004- Personalised Design-Ready-`**; without it → held (not written). Item Name **Custom**, **Customisable**, and **Customised** are whole words (locked 2026-10-14); `Personali` stays a substring. **Blank ship-by → today** (run date; locked 2026-09-24). Unparseable **non-blank** ship-by → `UNMATCHED`. **Hashim #037:** Shift 1 **order** volume **above 300** → leftover CSVs split today vs later dates; ≤300 leftover may mix. **Fixed batches stay one CSV per code per shift** (locked 2026-10-08). Do **not** dump overflow into Shift 2/3. 1st and 2nd write today and overdue. **Nth `--run` of the day = nth shift** (`SHIFT_PER_RUN`, locked 2026-10-14). **3rd shift and later** write overdue, blank, and the run-day ship-by, plus tag `1004- Personalised Design-Ready-` when ship-by is later (locked 2026-10-22). A later ship-by without that tag stays in `awaiting_shipment`. Ignore SS shift tags. Whole order stays together.

## Names

On-disk filename is **six fields only** (grouping logic unchanged): `S{n}-{PLAIN|PRINTED}-{1|2}-{WAREHOUSE STOCK|SUPPLY ON DEMAND|IN HOUSE MANUFACTURE}-{R|P}-{priority}`. Shift is field 1 (after batch `B` prefix). Prime=`1`, non-prime=`2`. Customised `P`, readymade `R`. **Fixed batches first** — codes and priority live in `database/order-grouping-sorter/fixed_batches.csv` (row order = first match wins; dry-run reports `fixed-batch overlaps`). **Leftover** — plain piles `B2000`/`B2100`/`B2200`/`B2500`/`B2600`/`B2700`/…; printed piles `B1`/`B2`/…; both skip reserved numbers. Example filename: `B100-S1-PRINTED-2-WAREHOUSE STOCK-R-5`. Example PIN: `B100-S1-1 Item 1`. Those skip the 30-chain. Leftover still splits on Graph + 30-chain; peel values are not in the filename. **Priority** (per shift): today first, then prime first, then as files are made. Catalog-miss `RESEND` / `UNMATCHED` have no `B` slots. Resend product batches use `B9000` / `B9050` / `B9040` / `B9100` / `B9150` / `B9200`. MAS Clothing → `fawad`; other stores → `own`. Prime = SS tag `Amazon Prime Order`.

Packing PIN / PDF: `{B}-S{n}-{process_number} Item {item}` — only batch code + shift from the filename (e.g. filename `B100-S1-PRINTED-2-WAREHOUSE STOCK-R-1` → `B100-S1-1 Item 1`). Process Number Tracker is off.

Leftover (non-fixed) piles get `B1`, `B2`, … skipping reserved fixed-batch numbers. Inside the batch: colour ≥3 units → own process number first; then 50-unit process numbers; same order stays on one process number. Packs skip colour groups (50-unit process numbers only).

`--run` writes one CSV per process into Packing Input. **Testing:** `1st Shift` every `--run`. `RESEND.csv` / `UNMATCHED.csv` land there.
